<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>VLA performance on the Calvin <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mees et al., 2022</a>)</cite> benchmark with and without wrist-view generation. We use the Video Prediction Policy (VPP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> as our VLA.
In Calvin, each episode consists of five sequential tasks and terminates once a failure occurs.
The columns 1/5–5/5 report success rates of completing at least <math id="S3.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> tasks in sequence, while <em id="S3.T2.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Avg. Len.</em> denotes the mean number of tasks completed per episode. </figcaption>
</figure>
